WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.317
AI could break

00:00:01.128 --> 00:00:02.472
encryption before quantum

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:02.908
does

00:00:03.438 --> 00:00:04.511
A new danger

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:05.395
captured attention

00:00:05.207 --> 00:00:05.855
this week

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:07.364
AI labs might

00:00:07.176 --> 00:00:08.567
unleash an ultimate

00:00:08.379 --> 00:00:09.428
decryption event

00:00:09.629 --> 00:00:10.890
factoring the huge

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:11.857
numbers that guard

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:12.388
our data

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.714
Classic RSA security

00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:15.881
rests on multiplying

00:00:15.705 --> 00:00:16.801
two big primes

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:17.544
into a figure

00:00:17.356 --> 00:00:18.322
of two thousand

00:00:18.134 --> 00:00:19.053
forty-eight bits

00:00:19.231 --> 00:00:20.433
about six hundred

00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:22.002
seventeen decimal digits

00:00:22.526 --> 00:00:23.787
The FT argues

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:24.943
for faster upgrades

00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:25.651
to security

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:27.007
not panic and

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:27.761
for disclosing

00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:29.731
verifying and discussing

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.004
any breakthrough openly

00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:32.556
Full story on

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:33.263
the dashboard
